WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.918
A 27B model

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.227
shrunk to 7.2

00:00:03.039 --> 00:00:04.418
gigabytes no math

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:04.901
lost

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:06.691
LookAtMyQuant is a

00:00:06.503 --> 00:00:08.024
quantization compiler

00:00:07.836 --> 00:00:08.814
that measures how

00:00:08.626 --> 00:00:09.557
much each part

00:00:09.369 --> 00:00:10.099
of a model

00:00:09.911 --> 00:00:10.889
hurts output when

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:11.479
compressed

00:00:11.645 --> 00:00:12.776
then spends bits

00:00:12.588 --> 00:00:13.543
where they matter

00:00:14.062 --> 00:00:15.288
It takes Qwen3

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:15.606
.

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:18.342
8-27B from 53.7

00:00:18.154 --> 00:00:19.922
gigabytes to 7.2

00:00:20.135 --> 00:00:21.220
and still solves

00:00:21.031 --> 00:00:23.283
401 of 540

00:00:23.095 --> 00:00:24.097
math problems

00:00:24.215 --> 00:00:25.170
as many as

00:00:24.982 --> 00:00:25.819
the original

00:00:26.342 --> 00:00:27.580
Inkling 2 Mini

00:00:27.392 --> 00:00:28.476
gets six Apple

00:00:28.288 --> 00:00:29.254
Silicon builds

00:00:29.302 --> 00:00:31.023
from 3.85 to

00:00:30.835 --> 00:00:32.757
12.76 gigabytes

00:00:32.946 --> 00:00:33.865
reaching down to

00:00:33.689 --> 00:00:35.245
8 gigabyte iPhones

00:00:35.766 --> 00:00:36.780
Full story on

00:00:36.591 --> 00:00:37.487
the dashboard
